            <div xml:id="d728">

                <pb facs="0874" n="772" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg772"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.672/548: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commission in Turkey to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-23T13:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 23,
                                1927—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>12. Department’s telegram No. 14, January 21 [<hi rendition="#italic">22</hi>], 1
                    p.m. The Government organ <hi rendition="#italic">Milliyet</hi>, and the
                    semiofficial paper <hi rendition="#italic">Djumhuriet</hi>, <pb facs="0875"
                        n="773" xml:id="pg773"/> print editorials today which are believed to be
                    strongly indicative of Turkish official opinion. The <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Milliyet</hi> states: “Our attitude will be one of dignified indifference.”
                    The <hi rendition="#italic">Djumhuriet</hi> urges that Americans be not made the
                    object of any treatment which is different from that applied to all other
                    countries; and states that Turkish circles are convinced that the rejection of
                    the treaty by the United States Senate is a mere accident. Since my telegram No.
                    11, January 21, 6 p.m., all press comment has been distinctly conciliatory and
                    friendly, and this attitude has been assumed by such Turkish officials I have
                    met, including the Chairman of the Committee on Foreign Affairs of the Grand
                    National Assembly.</p>
                <p>All telegrams received from the Department or which are sent by me, are being
                    sent immediately to Angora to the High Commissioner.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crosby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
